\label{thm:dynamic-upper}
	There is a randomized single-pass streaming algorithm that for integers $q,t \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, given any multi-graph $G=(V,E)$ with $\mbox{\rm poly}(n)$ edge multiplicities in a dynamic stream, 
	with high probability, distinguishes between $\chi(G) \leqslant q$ vs $\chi(G) \geqslant q \cdot t$ in $\ensuremath{\widetilde{O}}(n^2/t^2)$ space.

