	Any randomized single-pass streaming algorithm that for $3 \leqslant q \leqslant \mbox{\rm poly}\!\log{(n)}$ and any $t \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, given any multi-graph $G=(V,E)$ with $O(n)$ edge multiplicities in a dynamic stream, 
	with high constant probability distinguishes between $\chi(G) \leqslant q$ vs $\chi(G) \geqslant q \cdot t$ requires $\ensuremath{\widetilde{\Omega}}(n^2/t^2)$ space.

